{"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"KeyboardKit"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"AI Support","images":[{"identifier":"Feature-AI.jpg","type":"card"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/AI-Article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Features-Articles"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"This article describes the KeyboardKit AI support capabilities.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Apple’s native keyboard APIs lack many features that are needed when building AI-based keyboards, for instance being able to read the entire text document or letting users type text within the keyboard extension.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Important","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"👑 KeyboardKit Pro unlocks many AI-supporting features. You can sign up for KeyboardKit Pro from the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/keyboardkit.com"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"},{"text":"Document Reader","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Document-Reader"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Apple’s native ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/UIKit\/UITextDocumentProxy","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" doesn’t return all the text within the document. It cuts off the available text at any time, e.g. at the previous or next paragraph, which makes it hard to provide AI-based features that require more context.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit Pro therefore unlocks a set of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/UIKit\/UITextDocumentProxy\/fullDocumentContext(config:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" text document proxy extensions that let you read ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"all","type":"text"}]},{"text":" text from the current document, by moving the input cursor:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let proxy = controllerContext.textDocumentProxy","let result = try await proxy.fullDocumentContext()"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This returns a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/TextDocumentReaderResult","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" with the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/TextDocumentReaderResult\/fullDocumentContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", as well as separate properties for the text before and after the text input cursor.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Proxy-Article","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" article for more information.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Next Word Prediction","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Next-Word-Prediction"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Apple’s native text prediction utilities stopped supporting next word prediction in iOS 16. Instead, it only provides predictions on already typed text, without any (known) way to get next word predictions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit Pro therefore unlocks ways to perform next word prediction with Apple’s Foundation Models (iPhone 15 Pro and later), or with 3rd party services like ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/AutocompleteMethod\/claude","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/AutocompleteMethod\/openAI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for more complex predictions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Autocomplete-Article","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" article for more information and important considerations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Text Input Components","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Text-Input-Components"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Apple’s native input controller and text document proxy don’t let you type in text fields within a keyboard extensions. Even if a text field is focused in the keyboard, text is sent to the main app. This makes it hard to let user perform AI-based prompting within the keyboard.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit Pro therefore unlocks a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardTextField","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" that automatically manages in-keyboard typing, without any extra code:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct MyView: View {","","    @EnvironmentObject var context: KeyboardControllerContext","","    @State var text = \"\"","","    var body: some View {","        KeyboardTextField(","            text: $text, ","            context: context","        )","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The keyboard-specific text components will automatically manage text routing and only take proxy ownership while they are focused.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/TextInput-Article"},{"text":" article for more information.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion"